      "problem": "$\\int \\operatorname{sech}⁡y(5\\operatorname{tanh}⁡y-\\operatorname{sech}⁡y)\\text{d}y=$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\operatorname{sech}⁡y)=-\\operatorname{sech}⁡y\\operatorname{tanh}⁡y & \\,⇒\\,\\int \\operatorname{sech}⁡y\\operatorname{tanh}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y=-\\operatorname{sech}⁡y+C, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡y)={sech}^{2}⁡y & \\,⇒\\,\\int {sech}^{2}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y=\\operatorname{tanh}⁡y+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\operatorname{sech}⁡y(5\\operatorname{tanh}⁡y-\\operatorname{sech}⁡y)\\text{d}y & =\\int (5\\operatorname{sech}⁡y\\operatorname{tanh}⁡y-{sech}^{2}⁡y)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =5\\int \\operatorname{sech}⁡y\\operatorname{tanh}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y-\\int {sech}^{2}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =-5\\operatorname{sech}⁡y-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡y+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
